te]} {:db/id "q-109156" :question/id #uuid "d402a78d-7baa-5a8f-a1ce-6df24cc00d98" :question/math-academy-id "q-109156" :question/problem "If $x=5{y}^{3}-10{y}^{2},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(5{y}^{3}-10{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-10\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =15{y}^{2}-20y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{15{y}^{2}-20y}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109156/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00ac6edc-908a-50be-9ef1-4b24ba597d1d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109156"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-312549/field-1/fbe5c87a49b7a0750f3fa9394a473954e82eb612cd9bcb9d995458ea0895ebfa" :answer/id #uuid "fa2dd8fb-895c-5f4e-94bd-f5b301271f50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2y-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-312549/field-1/7fdc67f8e7bd16301a2ed903d1deb3605c8d784ed7de7643365f34687dd10677" :answer/id #uuid "134140fd-453d-5b29-9d53-1b1ecc5b01dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2y-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-312549/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "87ca3907-14b7-5e18-b658-b106098cb838" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-312549/field-1/fbe5c87a49b7a0750f3fa9394a473954e82eb612cd9bcb9d995458ea0895ebfa" :answer-field/choices ["q-312549/field-1/fbe5c87a49b7a0750f3fa9394a473954e82eb612cd9bcb9d995458ea0895ebfa" "q-312549/field-1/7fdc67f8e7bd16301a2ed903d1deb3605c8d784ed7de7643365f34687dd10677"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-312549" :question/id #uuid "c4724076-8252-5361-8cdf-8e30f8695953" :question/math-academy-id "q-312549" :question/problem "Given that $x={y}^{2}-y,$ express $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ as a function of $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}-y) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y) \\\\  & =2y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2y-1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-312549/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00ac6edc-908a-50be-9ef1-4b24ba597d1d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-312549"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341608/field-1/f8e4f4591569b54157d9e13f817186d4028944afa5d5e59c9fbb43ce97a021c6" :answer/id #uuid "c37f9256-da8a-5ba7-bd60-ed511c831190" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4+10y^4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341608/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "97d53035-97e0-582c-afb0-253e72579b34" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341608/field-1/f8e4f4591569b54157d9e13f817186d4028944afa5d5e59c9fbb43ce97a021c6" :answer-field/choices ["q-341608/field-1/f8e4f4591569b54157d9e13f817186d4028944afa5d5e59c9fbb43ce97a021c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341608" :question/id #uuid "05897e0d-06be-55d9-88a0-39032be05a4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-341608" :question/problem "Given that $x=-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+5{y}^{2},$ express $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ as a function of $y.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | ${y}^{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+5{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-2{y}^{-1}+5{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2})+5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2(-2{y}^{-3})+5(2y) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}+10y \\\\  & =\\frac{4+10{y}^{4}}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+10{y}^{4}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-341608/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00ac6edc-908a-50be-9ef1-4b24ba597d1d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341608"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-32705"] :question/problem "If $x=-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+2{y}^{2},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}+2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-2{y}^{-2}+2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =4{y}^{-3}+4y \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{y}^{3}}+4y \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4{y}^{4}}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{4+4{y}^{4}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-170132/selection/e118d04a87bf77c40ec9c864ebea3dff2886761d4a9a0d7b36f54808b1b6599d" :answer/id #uuid "ffd78458-d203-54e5-940d-600f84a02ff6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9{y}^{2}-20{y}^{4}}" :db/ensure [:an