-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(3{y}^{3}-4{y}^{5}) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{5}) \\\\  & =9{y}^{2}-20{y}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{9{y}^{2}-20{y}^{4}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-170132/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00ac6edc-908a-50be-9ef1-4b24ba597d1d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-170132"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-51336/selection/9f600c666fb656b4a7c8d9047db6891453f972982bbc52a1a1104970b8a2cb4e" :answer/id #uuid "9f6dad1d-e156-5684-b74e-101cfc0b0d5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51336/selection/7e978c54170214b26427b3c2b51ec4318a6f72efb4904214de6989347746ebe9" :answer/id #uuid "e8033fcd-d134-5dad-b539-cb7edfc6631a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51336/selection/2aef90071200a7bc65baa2d03f49803233ca7b2dc16865265136281ee914878b" :answer/id #uuid "0e0f1a8c-0ef0-52c7-a098-fafd807d4a8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51336/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "f072ca5f-9a97-5334-affe-ea5072b01c04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51336/selection/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" :answer/id #uuid "e3e842ac-da9d-5a2e-b35d-3aa409a4b095" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-51336/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b4ee07f-34bd-5d6c-a0e6-0da499fa1149" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-51336/selection/2aef90071200a7bc65baa2d03f49803233ca7b2dc16865265136281ee914878b" :answer-field/choices ["q-51336/selection/9f600c666fb656b4a7c8d9047db6891453f972982bbc52a1a1104970b8a2cb4e" "q-51336/selection/7e978c54170214b26427b3c2b51ec4318a6f72efb4904214de6989347746ebe9" "q-51336/selection/2aef90071200a7bc65baa2d03f49803233ca7b2dc16865265136281ee914878b" "q-51336/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" "q-51336/selection/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-51336" :question/id #uuid "4928953b-0350-5f60-9789-334738000d33" :question/math-academy-id "q-51336" :question/problem "If $x=\\frac{2}{y}+\\frac{8}{{y}^{2}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(3,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{2}{y}+\\frac{8}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{-1}+8{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1})+8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-{y}^{-2})+8\\cdot (-2{y}^{-3}) \\\\  & =-2{y}^{-2}-16{y}^{-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{16}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2y-16}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2y+16}{{y}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2y+16}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(3,2),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(3,2)} & =-\\frac{{2}^{3}}{2(2)+16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{20} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-51336/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0305491f-5ac7-5ba4-9a80-1a9a79b964f0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-51336"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-170140/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "b82e4d60-7810-5484-ac36-49b2396d1af4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170140/selection/852df530a82e413447a8b733db5e62e6c70e6d0be8b2e885cd815d17a6fb4ba1" :answer/id #uuid "0b4a9813-c22d-5ac4-b345-e60feb489e09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170140/selection/edc901e84f0cdd5174afd49105ac3883566ea0e1e057217fb66083a56cc119ba" :answer/id #uuid "ddc48167-c772-5b74-bc36-f32d5ea63466" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170140/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "e76968bb-2549-5bb7-b324-4acdd4794389" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170140/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "8cc1cfa2-e77b-5df2-9230-d31b5ee7b961" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170140/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0d438b7-e840-53c5-9b8a-f6d144a45862" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-170140/selection/edc901e84f0cdd5174afd49105ac3883566ea0e1e057217fb66083a56cc119ba" :answer-field/choices ["q-170140/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-170140/selection/852df530a82e413447a8b733db5e62e6c70e6d0be8b2e885cd815d17a6fb4ba1" "q-170140/selection/edc901e84f0cdd5174afd49105ac3883566ea0e1e057217fb66083a56cc119ba" "q-170140/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-170140/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-170140" :question/id #uuid "bbe5e0e9-59cc-550d-aeef-7d41dc23e22b" :question/math-academy-id "q-170140" :question/problem "If $x=y-2{y}^{3},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y-2{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3}) \\\\  & =1-6{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{1-6{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(1,-1),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(1,-1)} & =\\frac{1}{1-6(-1)^{2}}=-\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-170140/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0305491f-5ac7-5ba4-9a80-1a9a79b964f0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-170140"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341757/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "e2f80c6c-fdf9-588b-b84f-6a0f3d1a089a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341757/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5cd43bec-34df-53b7-b316-a53d2403a1e4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341757/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer-field/choices ["q-341757/field-1/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341757" :question/id #uuid "aada2aac-9808-566e-a932-6ee841bb6da4" :question/math-academy-id "q-341757" :question/problem "If $x=-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{y}}-2y\\sqrt{y},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at the point $(-14,1).$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-14,1)}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{y}}-2y\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-12{y}^{-1/2}-2y\\cdot {y}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(-12{y}^{-1/2}-2{y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =-12\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1/2})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =-12(-\\frac{1}{2}){y}^{-3/2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{y}^{1/2} \\\\  & =6{y}^{-3/2}-3{y}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{y\\sqrt{y}}-3\\sqrt{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-3{y}^{2}}{y\\sqrt{y}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{y\\sqrt{y}}{6-3{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(-14,1),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-14,1)} & =\\frac{1\\sqrt{1}}{6-3(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-341757/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0305491f-5ac7-5ba4-9a80-1a9a79b964f0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341757"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186120126 :question/answer-fields 17592186117276] {:db/id "q-32595/selection/ma-v1/6d9c7f6e99ce78d4454c80ab5f86a5beac40ad41013689d717e5707b4f346890/b107f74a4e16c10bb036368b88d19850ac85381660f8b8712359b4d1eac94915" :answer/id #uuid "f466adf4-43d5-56da-851f-a6e555037c73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32595/select