oblem "Given a curve $x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}-2{y}^{2},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-1,1)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}-2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1/2})-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-3/2}-2\\cdot (2y) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{y}^{3/2}}-4y \\\\  & =\\frac{-1-8{y}^{5/2}}{2{y}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1+8{y}^{2}\\sqrt{y}}{2y\\sqrt{y}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=-\\frac{2y\\sqrt{y}}{1+8{y}^{2}\\sqrt{y}}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(-1,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(-1,1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2(1)\\sqrt{1}}{1+8(1)^{2}\\sqrt{1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =-\\frac{2}{9}(x-(-1)) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{9}x-\\frac{2}{9}+1 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{9}x+\\frac{7}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-170190/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ff302ba-5a3f-599b-b038-7417af1dca71"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-170190"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-32596"] :question/problem "Given a curve $x=\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}-{y}^{2},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(9,3)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 3{y}^{2}-2y \\\\  & =2{y}^{2}-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2{y}^{2}-2y}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(9,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(9,3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2(3)^{2}-2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{1}{12}(x-9) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{12}-\\frac{3}{4}+3 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{12}+\\frac{9}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-342049/field-1/a2bfd2a5d500209d7a1a071a416e152210527ec3d6747089a0bd24db30d7231c" :answer/id #uuid "90531a37-fc9e-5c9f-a16f-88465b373949" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3x}{8}+\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342049/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "610faf0f-7729-5522-893e-0781abd865f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342049/field-1/a2bfd2a5d500209d7a1a071a416e152210527ec3d6747089a0bd24db30d7231c" :answer-field/choices ["q-342049/field-1/a2bfd2a5d500209d7a1a071a416e152210527ec3d6747089a0bd24db30d7231c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342049" :question/id #uuid "45e88e0a-eda2-5d07-9063-d301368f5fe4" :question/math-academy-id "q-342049" :question/problem "Given a curve $x=2y-\\frac{6}{y},$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,3)?$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2y-\\frac{6}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2y-6{y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)-6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1}) \\\\  & =2(1)-6(-{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2+6{y}^{-2} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{6}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{y}^{2}+6}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2{y}^{2}+6}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,3)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(4,3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{2(3)^{2}+6} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{3}{8}\\cdot (x-4) \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{8}x-\\frac{3}{2}+3 \\\\ y & =\\frac{3}{8}x+\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342049/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ff302ba-5a3f-599b-b038-7417af1dca71"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342049"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110192/selection/453a3b4b674fd79fce429be7d704a9f86c161f340678163b992e82c66115b2c6" :answer/id #uuid "9cf3f0f0-a6ce-5d6c-a030-c21bec510897" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110192/selection/0eab2efc7ea920a43a6e0db9dd8e76187d96482975c6ba35a3bbbffeecdf87ae" :answer/id #uuid "ad4c99bb-8b6d-5c67-b6c4-90de5961e269" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{18}-\\frac{7}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110192/selection/c9c85e530c183be00bbe134d18562a1866e156e0a095120463f8893169b033a2" :answer/id #uuid "e2ccaf33-86cc-52d8-b71c-5f6edbaa24b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{16}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110192/selection/ad82ae054b9b9b8a53b009531d770a8dcd8273194d95a1af42284f9fde9511ad" :answer/id #uuid "a1e323f8-7582-56ac-a835-3a7822270a75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{8}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110192/selection/8ed98d92c496deec02ff8683e7499f50df89dd50996f85ed32284e5ae3460149" :answer/id #uuid "1fc6a547-b739-57dc-a6b9-8a02dc338d22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{8}-\\frac{8}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110192/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1cfa6d9-bc03-5e11-a377-d13e974df5f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110192/selection/ad82ae054b9b9b8a53b009531d770a8dcd8273194d95a1af42284f9fde9511ad" :answer-field/choices ["q-110192/selection/453a3b4b674fd79fce429be7d704a9f86c161f340678163b992e82c66115b2c6" "q-110192/selection/0eab2efc7ea920a43a6e0db9dd8e76187d96482975c6ba35a3bbbffeecdf87ae" "q-110192/selection/c9c85e530c183be00bbe134d18562a1866e156e0a095120463f8893169b033a2" "q-110192/selection/ad82ae054b9b9b8a53b009531d770a8dcd8273194d95a1af42284f9fde9511ad" "q-110192/selection/8ed98d92c496deec02ff8683e7499f50df89dd50996f85ed32284e5ae3460149"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110192" :question/id #uuid "eb002c1f-25a0-5470-9804-c9c0192129f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-110192" :question/problem "Given a curve $x=5{y}^{3}-8{y}^{2}+16,$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(24,2)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(5{y}^{3}-8{y}^{2}+16) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+16\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =5\\cdot (3{y}^{2})-8\\cdot (2y)+0 \\\\  & =15{y}^{2}-16y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{15{y}^{2}-16y}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(24,2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(24,2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15\\cdot {2}^{2}-16\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{28}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-2 & =\\frac{1}{28}(x-24) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{28}-\\frac{6}{7}+2 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{8}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-110192/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ff302ba-5a3f-599b-b038-7417af1dca71"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110192"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-170192/selection/3f8c2b81af03f567624bd5fe0fde48670612d85e8de8f5775c44067c63772fb2" :answer/id #uuid "a0a557f9-6a8c-51f4-b4d1-4039834ac6f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170192/selection/67245d042331fd1b54b6c80d17c5c11f7c67e3c192d3145a09173be67dc88b34" :answer/id #uuid "c1f557ce-2eea-585f-80db-e54a1453d899" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170192/selection/e71640b532bee6a1311440f9b2b03da10cc7e2c75e7a4c1940537021919ef96a" :answer/id #uuid "eee2b696-a3a6-59d4-8e91-da93d36cff2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=6x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170192/selection/1ed377d962d3f5d6d3ad9e86fd6f19fa40d1bfcd75a2319ddfcb1395240b84b3" :answer/id #uuid "37be0d41-97a3-58d9-8233-f02797fba6a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=6x-23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170192/selection/0a6ad83e9b19c722f6dca7d687ebb1cf6b59e4648479999ddb32cfb041904676" :answer/id #uuid "b74db806-be40-57af-a1b7-dc43cc750755" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{23}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170192/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bce113ae-7d3a-5121-b63f-cc4d2e99513e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-170192/selection/67245d042331fd1b54b6c80d17c5c11f7c67e3c192d3145a09173be67dc88b34" :answer-field/choices ["q-170192/selection/3f8c2b81af03f567624bd5fe0fde48670612d85e8de8f5775c44067c63772fb2" "q-170192/selection/67245d042331fd1b54b6c80d17c5c11f7c67e3c192d3145a09173be67dc88b34" "q-170192/selection/e71640b532bee6a1311440f9b2b03da10cc7e2c75e7a4c1940537021919ef96a" "q-170192/selection/1ed377d962d3f5d6d3ad9e86fd6f19fa40d1bfcd75a2319ddfcb1395240b84b3" "q-170192/selection/0a6ad83e9b19c722f6dca7d687ebb1cf6b59e4648479999ddb32cfb041904676"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-170192" :question/id #uuid "9d13262e-5677-5318-bc1a-cd98d393d979" :question/math-academy-id "q-170192" :question/problem "Given a curve $x=4{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}-1,$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,1)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(4{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}-1) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (2y)-2{y}^{-3}-0 \\\\  & =8y-\\frac{2}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8{y}^{4}-2}{{y}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{8{y}^{4}-2}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(4,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1)^{3}}{8(1)^{4}-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =\\frac{1}{6}(x-4) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{6}-\\frac{2}{3}+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{6}+\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-170192/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ff302ba-5a3f-599b-b038-7417af1dca71"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-170192"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12467"] :question/problem "If $x=2y^2 + \\dfrac1{y^2}$, then find $\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{2}+{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =4y-2{y}^{-3} \\\\  & =4y-\\frac{2}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{y}^{4}-2}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac{y^3}{4y^4 -2}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12468"] :question/problem "If $x = y + 2y\\sqrt y$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx}$ at the point $\\left(3 , 1\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y+2y\\sqrt{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y+2{y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =1+2\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =1+3{y}^{1/2} \\\\  & =1+3\\sqrt{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} =  \\dfrac{1}{1 + 3\\sqrt y}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(3,1),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(3,1)} & =\\frac{1}{1+3\\sqrt{1}}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12469"] :question/problem "What is the equation of the tangent to the curve $x = 2y^2 -y + 1$ at the point $(2,1)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{2}-y+1) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(y)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (2y)-1+0 \\\\  & =4y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm dx} = \\left( \\dfrac{\\textrm dx}{\\textrm dy} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac1{4y - 1}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(2,1)$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(2,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4(1)-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =\\frac{1}{3}(x-2) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
